const e="townsville-eisteddfod-vocal",u=2026,o="Read the whole 2026 vocal syllabus (rules and 41 sections). It prints no entry fees, entry dates, venue name or address, contact people or news, so those sections and variables are empty. It prints no points, grades or judging criteria. The stage size, choir limit and risers are edition facts kept as variables. The Own Choice document form is described, not copied.",n={Title:"Vocal Rules & Conditions",Subtitle:"Townsville Eisteddfod 2026 vocal sections: choirs, solos, duets and ensembles",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"All vocal sections are Own Choice. Check the syllabus for changes before you enter. Time limits are printed for every section.",Notes:["The syllabus is marked 'check for changes': the organiser may change a section before the event.","Adjudicator: {{Adjudicator}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General rules",Items:["All vocal sections are Own Choice (rule 2).","Classical repertoire is a serious composition with artistic merit, excluding jazz or popular idiom. Music from any century is accepted. It may be sung in the original language or in English (rule 3).","Time limits are printed against each section and are part of the section.","The syllabus is headed 'check for changes'. Look for changes before you enter.","Adjudicator for 2026: {{Adjudicator}}.","The stage is {{StageSize}}. Only groups competing in the relevant section may sit in the auditorium (rule 1l)."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who may enter",Items:["Choirs: entries are limited to one choir per school per section (rule 1a).","A choir, group or ensemble entered as a School Choir, Group or Ensemble must be made up only of bona fide current students of the school named (rule 1d).","No member of one choir or group may perform with another choir, group or ensemble in the same section (rule 1e).","All children must be under school staff supervision at all times while in the theatre (rule 1b).","Age and school-year limits are printed per section: for example Senior Choral Championship age 18 and under, Middle School Year 9 and under, Primary Year 6 and under, Junior Primary Year 4 and under; solos by single age or age band; duets and the Vocal Ensemble age 18 and under, or as printed.","Vocal Bursary: open to any Townsville competitor aged 15 to 18 who, in the opinion of the adjudicator, shows the most potential. The competitor must have competed in the Vocal Championship."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Choirs, duets and ensembles",Items:["A choir may have at most {{ChoirMaxVoices}} voices. Backing tracks are not allowed for choirs (rule 1).","Where solo parts are specified in choral sections, the parts so marked are to be performed together by the whole of that voice section of the choir (rule 1c).","Choir risers are provided: {{ChoirRisers}} (rule 1f).","Teams are entered as choirs, duets or ensembles in the Team groups of the template."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"Own Choice document",Items:["Complete the 2026 Own Choice Document for the Chairperson before you arrive at the venue. It is read aloud before the performance. Check that the details are accurate and legible.","Attach one Own Choice Document to each entry. It is needed for all vocal and all instrumental entries (except Digital Piano), and for speech and drama: all drama (including prepared mime) and character poem only.","The form asks for: section number, competitor's name, title of work, and, for Musical Theatre items only, the source musical.","For Digital Piano entries only, two completed forms are required for each piece."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Staging and accompaniment",Items:["Accompaniment: Piano only for Classical Vocal Solos, Classical Duets and the Choral Chief Chorus. A backing track with no vocals is optional for all other sections, except Self-Accompanied Vocal Solo and all Choral sections (rule 4a).","A single instrument other than piano may accompany Unison Chorus, Modern Chorus, Novelty Chorus, Folk Singing, Vocal Ensemble, Solo from Musical and Music Theatre Duet, Novelty Vocal Solo and Duet, Vocal Trio, and Modern Pop and Modern Pop Duo (rule 4b).","Competitors must find their own accompanists. One piano is available (rule 4c).","A looper pedal with the competitor's own amplifier may be used with a guitar in Self-Accompanied Vocal Solo (rule 4d).","Piano is on centre stage for all sections except: Novelty Chorus, Novelty Solo and Duet, Solo from Musical and Musical Theatre Duet, which use the side stage (second wing OP). For all choral sections except Novelty Chorus the piano is beside the risers (rule 5).","Curtain: optional for Musical Theatre Solo and Duet and Novelty Chorus only. Tell the Marshall before the start of the section (rule 6).","Costumes and hand-held props: optional for Novelty Chorus, Musical Theatre Solo and Duet, Novelty Solo and Duet, and Film or TV only (rule 7).","Microphone: optional for Modern Pop Solo and Duet, Film or TV Solo and Self-Accompanied Vocal Solo only (rule 8).","Choirs enter and leave the stage from the auditorium, except Novelty Chorus and Vocal Ensemble, who may enter from backstage (rule 1k)."]},{Key:"points",Title:"Championships and scoring",Items:["One set of trophies is awarded for each Choral Championship on combined marks (Choral Championship sections).","Scores must be clearly marked on the front with C (Chief) and A (Australian) or U (Unison), and numbered 1 or 2 to show the performance order. All songs must be performed.","Chief: appropriate championship standard. Senior and Middle Chief need at least two parts. Primary and Junior Primary Chief may be unison or partwork, with piano accompaniment only.","Australian: the work must not be a folk song arranged by an Australian musician. It may be unison or partwork, with piano or a single instrument and non-amplified instruments designated in the score, played by bona fide members of the choir."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Vocal awards",Items:["Vocal Bursary (see Who may enter).","Awards named in the syllabus: Most Outstanding Vocal Item; Most Outstanding Choir; Most Outstanding Musical Theatre Item; Most Outstanding Classical Vocalist; Most Promising Vocalist age 12 to 18; Encouragement for Vocalist age 11 and under; Most Promising Male Vocalist; Young Accompanist Encouragement age 25 and under."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Other parts of the eisteddfod",Items:["Instrumental, piano, speech and drama sections are covered by other syllabi and are not part of this template."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Vocal Syllabus 2026 (PDF)",Url:"https://townsvilleeisteddfod.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Vocal-Syllabus-2026.pdf"}]},a=[],t=[],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Choral Championship","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 1 to 4","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["10 minutes in total per choir."],"Rules":["Each choir performs a Chief Chorus and a choral work by an Australian composer. All songs must be performed.","Scores are marked C (Chief) and A (Australian) and numbered 1 or 2 for the performance order.","One set of trophies is awarded for each championship on combined marks."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Combined marks of the two works decide the championship."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 10 minutes in total per choir.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each choir performs a Chief Chorus and a choral work by an Australian composer. All songs must be performed.\\n- Scores are marked C (Chief) and A (Australian) and numbered 1 or 2 for the performance order.\\n- One set of trophies is awarded for each championship on combined marks.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Combined marks of the two works decide the championship."},{"Title":"Unison Chorus","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, section 5","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["Year 6 and under. Choir risers are set. Piano or single instrument accompaniment only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Year 6 and under. Choir risers are set. Piano or single instrument accompaniment only."},{"Title":"Modern Chorus","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, section 6","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["Partwork, age 18 and under. Choir risers are set. Piano or single instrument accompaniment only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Partwork, age 18 and under. Choir risers are set. Piano or single instrument accompaniment only."},{"Title":"Novelty Chorus","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 7 and 8","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["6 minutes."],"Rules":["Year 6 and under (section 7); Open Novelty Chorus age 18 and under (section 8).","Choir risers are optional and may be removed. Competitors may enter and leave from backstage or the auditorium; give instructions to the Marshall before the start of the section.","Piano or single instrument accompaniment, plus non-amplified instruments if designated in the score, played by bona fide members of the choir."],"Allowed":["Curtain, costumes and hand-held props."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 6 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Year 6 and under (section 7); Open Novelty Chorus age 18 and under (section 8).\\n- Choir risers are optional and may be removed. Competitors may enter and leave from backstage or the auditorium; give instructions to the Marshall before the start of the section.\\n- Piano or single instrument accompaniment, plus non-amplified instruments if designated in the score, played by bona fide members of the choir.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Curtain, costumes and hand-held props."},{"Title":"Folk Singing","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 9 and 10","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["Traditional unison or parts, Year 6 and under (section 9); traditional partwork, age 18 and under (section 10).","Songs must be from the traditional repertoire.","Piano or single instrument accompaniment, plus non-amplified instruments if designated in the score, played by bona fide members of the choir."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Traditional unison or parts, Year 6 and under (section 9); traditional partwork, age 18 and under (section 10).\\n- Songs must be from the traditional repertoire.\\n- Piano or single instrument accompaniment, plus non-amplified instruments if designated in the score, played by bona fide members of the choir."},{"Title":"Musical Theatre Vocal Solo","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 11 to 15","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["The song is from a stage musical, operetta or rock opera. Ages 18, 17, 16, 15 and 14 each have their own section.","The Own Choice Document must name the source musical."],"Allowed":["Curtain, costume and hand-held props. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The song is from a stage musical, operetta or rock opera. Ages 18, 17, 16, 15 and 14 each have their own section.\\n- The Own Choice Document must name the source musical.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Curtain, costume and hand-held props. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."},{"Title":"Novelty Vocal Solo","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 16 to 19","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes for age 11 to 13; 2 minutes 30 seconds for age 10, age 9 and age 8 and under."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":["Costume and hand-held props."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes for age 11 to 13; 2 minutes 30 seconds for age 10, age 9 and age 8 and under.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costume and hand-held props."},{"Title":"Modern Pop Vocal Solo","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 20 to 22","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":["A microphone is optional. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A microphone is optional. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."},{"Title":"Vocal Solo from Film or TV","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 23 to 28","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes for age 16 to 18 and 13 to 15; 3 minutes for age 12, 11, 10 and 9 and under."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":["Costume, hand-held props and a microphone are optional."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes for age 16 to 18 and 13 to 15; 3 minutes for age 12, 11, 10 and 9 and under.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costume, hand-held props and a microphone are optional."},{"Title":"Self-Accompanied Vocal Solo","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 29 and 30","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["The singer accompanies themselves. A backing track is not allowed in this section."],"Allowed":["A looper pedal with the competitor's own amplifier may be used with a guitar. A microphone is optional."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The singer accompanies themselves. A backing track is not allowed in this section.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A looper pedal with the competitor's own amplifier may be used with a guitar. A microphone is optional."},{"Title":"Classical Vocal Championship","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, section 31","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["Age 15 to 18. Piano accompaniment only. Classical repertoire."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Age 15 to 18. Piano accompaniment only. Classical repertoire."},{"Title":"Classical Vocal Solo","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 32 to 35","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes for age 16 to 18; 3 minutes for age 14 and 15, 11 to 13, and 10 and under."],"Rules":["Piano accompaniment only. Classical repertoire."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes for age 16 to 18; 3 minutes for age 14 and 15, 11 to 13, and 10 and under.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Piano accompaniment only. Classical repertoire."},{"Title":"Novelty Vocal Duet","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, sections 36 to 38","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Harmony or unison. Age 18 and under, 12 and under, and 10 and under."],"Allowed":["Costume and hand-held props. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Harmony or unison. Age 18 and under, 12 and under, and 10 and under.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costume and hand-held props. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."},{"Title":"Classical Vocal Duet","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, section 39","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Age 18 and under. Harmony must predominate. Piano accompaniment only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Age 18 and under. Harmony must predominate. Piano accompaniment only."},{"Title":"Musical Theatre Vocal Duet","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, section 40","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["Age 14 to 18. Stage or film musical, operetta or rock opera."],"Allowed":["Curtain, costume and hand-held props. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Age 14 to 18. Stage or film musical, operetta or rock opera.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Curtain, costume and hand-held props. A single instrument other than piano may accompany."},{"Title":"Vocal Ensemble","Source":"Vocal Sections 2026, section 41","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Age 18 and under. Maximum 16 singers. Harmony must predominate. Piano or single instrument accompaniment only. The ensemble may enter from backstage."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Age 18 and under. Maximum 16 singers. Harmony must predominate. Piano or single instrument accompaniment only. The ensemble may enter from backstage."}]`),s=[{Title:"Choral Championship",AgeGroup:"Team Year 4 & Under",Source:"Vocal Sections 2026, section 4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The Junior Primary Championship is a Chief Chorus and a Unison Chorus, not a work by an Australian composer."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The Junior Primary Championship is a Chief Chorus and a Unison Chorus, not a work by an Australian composer.`}],l=[{Key:"Adjudicator",Kind:"text",Label:"Adjudicator",Value:"Jonathon Welch AM, Brisbane",Source:"Vocal Rules & Conditions 2026, header"},{Key:"StageSize",Kind:"text",Label:"Stage dimensions",Value:"14.7 m x 11.8 m",Source:"Vocal Rules & Conditions 2026, rule 1h"},{Key:"ChoirMaxVoices",Kind:"text",Label:"Maximum voices in a choir",Value:"80",Source:"Vocal Rules & Conditions 2026, rule 1"},{Key:"ChoirRisers",Kind:"text",Label:"Choir risers provided",Value:"5 sets of 4 levels (plus floor)",Source:"Vocal Rules & Conditions 2026, rule 1f"}],r=[{Claim:"Rules, section conditions, time limits, accompaniment, staging and awards are from the organiser's own 2026 vocal syllabus.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Townsville Eisteddfod 2026 Vocal Rules & Conditions and Vocal Sections",Url:"https://townsvilleeisteddfod.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Vocal-Syllabus-2026.pdf"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:o,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:t,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:l,Evidence:r};export{t as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,r as Evidence,o as Note,n as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,l as Variables,u as Year,d as default};
